WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Drawing a block on an inclined plane with RustFig

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.600
The menus: File, Edit, View, Tools, Snap and Help

3
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.200
The name of the figure

4
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.800
The message panel says what to do next

5
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.400
The mouse indicator: what the left, middle and right buttons do right now

6
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.000
The units of the rulers

7
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.600
The mode panel: drawing modes at the top, editing modes below

8
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.200
The canvas, with its rulers

9
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.800
The indicator panel: the attributes of new objects

10
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.400
Depths and snapping

11
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.017
Polygon mode: the left button places the corners of the slope

12
00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:24.608
The middle button places the last corner and closes the polygon

13
00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:27.988
Go to mode: type part of a mode's name and press Enter

14
00:00:27.988 --> 00:00:32.218
Measure angle, middle button at the corner: it measures the angle and keeps it as the rotation angle

15
00:00:32.218 --> 00:00:35.948
Shift+middle draws the angle as an arc with its label

16
00:00:35.948 --> 00:00:40.412
Box mode: two left clicks at opposite corners

17
00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:43.872
Rotate counter-clockwise: the right button sets the center

18
00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:46.188
The left button turns the box by the measured angle, onto the slope

19
00:00:46.188 --> 00:00:52.957
Polyline mode, with a forward arrow set in the indicator panel

20
00:00:52.957 --> 00:00:58.989
The left button starts a line, the middle button ends it: the weight and the normal force

21
00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:07.955
Text mode with the TeX flag: the text is LaTeX, typeset on the canvas

22
00:01:07.955 --> 00:01:08.585
The middle button ends the text

23
00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:14.025
Text mode with the TeX flag: the text is LaTeX, typeset on the canvas

24
00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:19.718
Copy mode: pick the block with the left button, place the copy with another click

25
00:01:19.718 --> 00:01:23.303
Edit › Undo takes it back

26
00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:26.194
File › Save

27
00:01:26.194 --> 00:01:30.865
File › Export…: the PDF language is preselected, with the LaTeX typeset

28
00:01:30.865 --> 00:01:34.385
Export… asks where to save, then writes the PDF

29
00:01:34.385 --> 00:01:38.385
The PDF

